## Step 5: Author Content Slots and Help Content

Every user-visible string must be a content slot in English. Studio's AI translation handles all other locales.

```json
"contentSlots": [
  { "key": "searchLabel",    "kind": "label",       "description": "Accessible label for search input",        "default": "Search members" },
  { "key": "noResults",      "kind": "error",        "description": "Shown when search returns no results",     "default": "No members match your search." },
  { "key": "loadingMessage", "kind": "label",        "description": "Loading state message",                    "default": "Searching..." },
  { "key": "searchButton",   "kind": "action",       "description": "Search button label",                      "default": "Search" }
]
```

Add the `help` block — used by the AI Assistive Guidance context:

```json
"help": {
  "description": "Use Member Search to find a member by name or Medicaid ID.",
  "fields": {
    "placeholder": { "label": "Search term", "tooltip": "Enter a name, ID, or partial name" }
  },
  "aiHelpContext": {
    "componentOverview": "Member Search lets portal users find enrolled Medicaid members by name or ID. Returns paginated results with member status and coverage information.",
    "fields": {
      "placeholder": "The search input placeholder — shown when the field is empty."
    },
    "commonQuestions": ["How do I search by member ID?", "Can I search by date of birth?"],
    "limitations": "Returns only members enrolled in the current tenant's program. Does not search across tenants."
  }
}
```

**Rules:**
- All defaults and help text must be in English
- Every `contentSlot.key` should have a `help.fields` entry
- `aiHelpContext` is English-only and never rendered in the UI

