## Step 6: Declare Style Hooks

Declare every CSS custom property the component exposes for theming, plus any `::part()` selectors. Both light and dark themes must be supportable via these hooks.

```json
"styleHooks": [
  { "name": "--member-color-primary",    "kind": "cssVar", "description": "Primary accent color (button, highlight)" },
  { "name": "--member-color-background", "kind": "cssVar", "description": "Component background" },
  { "name": "--member-color-text",       "kind": "cssVar", "description": "Primary text color" },
  { "name": "--member-color-border",     "kind": "cssVar", "description": "Input and container border color" },
  { "name": "results-list",             "kind": "part",   "description": "Results container — exposes ::part(results-list)" },
  { "name": "search-input",             "kind": "part",   "description": "Search input — exposes ::part(search-input)" }
]
```

`styleHooks` entries **must** use `--<product>-*` prefixes (e.g. `--member-*`), not `--studio-*`. The `--studio-*` tokens are an optional overlay injected by Portal Studio — never the module's own API.

**In the component implementation:**
```css
.container {
  /* declare --<product>-* token with --studio-* as optional overlay fallback */
  --member-color-background: var(--studio-color-background, #ffffff);
  background: var(--member-color-background);
  --member-color-text: var(--studio-color-text, #2b3a44);
  color: var(--member-color-text);
}
button {
  --member-color-primary: var(--studio-color-primary, #2435C7);
  background: var(--member-color-primary);
}
.results {
  --member-color-border: var(--studio-color-border, #d5d8dc);
  border: 1px solid var(--member-color-border);
}
```

No hardcoded colors. Declare `--<product>-*` tokens on the root element; read `--studio-*` only as a fallback inside `var()`. Never declare a `--studio-*` property inside the component.

