## Step 9: Validate Before Publishing

Use the `studio_manifest` concern from `mmes-common-core` or the CLI:

**TypeScript:**
```typescript
import { validate } from '@mmes/core/studio_manifest';
import manifest from './studio-manifest.json';

const result = validate(JSON.stringify(manifest));
if (!result.valid) {
  console.error('Manifest validation failed:');
  result.errors.forEach(e => console.error(`  ${e.field}: ${e.message}`));
  process.exit(1);
}
console.log('✅ Manifest valid');
```

**CLI:**
```bash
studio-package-validator validate ./studio-manifest.json
```

Fix all errors before proceeding to publish. Never rely on the Studio compliance gate as the first validation step.

